      "writtenOn": "2025-03-03T20:56:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Despite resolving this offline, posting what I had drafted up:\n\nGood question - yes, originally I had it such that all render passes could potentially support reading from the dst as an input attachment.\n\nHowever, we can determine upfront if *no* draws in the DrawList need a dst read at renderpassdesc creation time. If that is the case, then we can take advantage of Vulkan image layouts optimized for different usages (i.e. `VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL`, `VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_SHADER_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL`, ...). This is as opposed to enforcing the usage of `VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_GENERAL` for the dst texture to accomodate being used as both the color attachment *and* as an input attachment.\n\nThis means renderpasses that **never** read from the dst can be optimized to use those layouts, but **renderpasses where ANY nonzero amount of draws read from the dst** can still be shared.\n\nThis still, however, enables us to compile the appropriate graphics pipeline when calling `DrawPass:prepareResources()` and will not lead to the \"surprise\" runtime creation of a pipeline when the cmd buffer issues draw commands. The RenderPass will know some draws read from the dst and some do not, so a pipeline for both will be created; though it would require a rebind which is unideal.",
      "parentUuid": "9b197258_ec902181",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 263
      },
      "revId": "bd72f72216e16a0c7954172955dc5c68dd547907",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
